// (1) What's the probability that the latency counter eventually reaches its max (20)?
// (1) Fires if state_operator_name = 1 -> triggers latency counter update
P=? [ F state_latency_counter = 20 ]

// (2) What's the probability that the opticflow counter reaches max (15)?
// (2) Fires if state_operator_name = 2 -> triggers opticflow counter update
P=? [ F state_opticflow_counter = 15 ]

// (3) Will the system eventually raise the check flag?
// (3) Can be triggered by either operator 1 or 2 -> updates check_flag on success
P=? [ F state_check_flag = true ]

// (4) Will the system eventually switch from hw-cybersickness-monitor to cybersickness-monitor?
// (4) Fires only if state_operator_name = 3 and check_flag = true
P=? [ F state_name = 1 ]

// (5) Is it guaranteed that the latency counter never exceeds 20?
// (5) Holds if counter update (from operator 1) respects upper bound
P>=1 [ G state_latency_counter <= 20 ]

// (6) Is it guaranteed that the opticflow counter never exceeds 15?
// (6) Holds if counter update (from operator 2) respects upper bound
P>=1 [ G state_opticflow_counter <= 15 ]

// (7) Is it always the case that check-flag is either true or false? (sanity property)
// (7) Always true due to check_flag being boolean (sanity check)
P>=1 [ G (state_check_flag = true | state_check_flag = false) ]

// (8) What’s the minimum probability of eventually reaching operator state apply-latency-violated?
// (8) Measures reachability of operator 1 (apply_latency_violated)
Pmin=? [ F state_operator_name = 1 ]

// (9) What’s the maximum probability of eventually reaching operator state apply-opticflow-violated?
// (9) Measures reachability of operator 2 (apply_opticflow_violated)
Pmax=? [ F state_operator_name = 2 ]


// PCTL Property File for cybersickness.prism

// Cybersickness monitor with phases and operator logic


// 1. LIVENESS: The system eventually assigns a cybersickness level
P=? [ F cybersickness_level_checked = true ]
// Eventually, the model reaches a state where the cybersickness level is computed.

// 2. TERMINATION: The model returns to propose phase after any apply
P>=1 [ G F phase = 0 ]
// From any state, the system eventually returns to phase = 0 (propose phase).

// 3. SWITCHING: The system eventually switches back to hardware monitor
P=? [ F state_name = 0 ]
// Probability that we eventually transition back to hardware monitoring mode.

// 4. BOUNDEDNESS: The sum value never exceeds ssq_high threshold
P>=1 [ G sum < ssq_high ]
// Ensures sum never exceeds 900 (no overflow or incorrect weight accumulation).

// 5. SAFETY: Sum is only calculated after all c1x1, c2x2, c3x3 are set
P>=1 [ G (! (cs_state_operator_name = 4) | (c1x1_set & c2x2_set & c3x3_set)) ]
// In all paths, at all times (G), if operator 4 is triggered, then the three weights must have been set.

// 6. CLASSIFICATION OUTCOME: Probability of ending in a specific cybersickness level
P=? [ F cybersickness_level = 0 ]  // Not affected
P=? [ F cybersickness_level = 1 ]  // Affected
P=? [ F cybersickness_level = 2 ]  // Incapacitated
// These show how likely the model is to classify the input into each level.

// 7. OPERATOR COVERAGE: Can each operator eventually be executed?
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 1 ]  // apply-c1x1
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 2 ]  // apply-c2x2
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 3 ]  // apply-c3x3
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 4 ]  // apply-sum-weights
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 5 ]  // apply-normal-level
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 6 ]  // apply-affected-level
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 7 ]  // apply-incapacitated-level
P=? [ F state_operator_name = 8 ]  // switch-monitor
// Checks if each operator can eventually become active during execution.

// 8. VALIDITY: cybersickness_level always stays in defined range
P>=1 [ G (cybersickness_level = 0 | cybersickness_level = 1 | cybersickness_level = 2) ]
// Prevents illegal state assignments.
